(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #153: each comparison, written both ways round, as the
 value of a declaration and of a Set at the top level.)

a number called heat is 4.
a number called limit is 6.

a boolean called 'heat matches' is heat is limit.
a boolean called 'limit matches' is limit is heat.
Print "is: {heat matches} {limit matches}".

a boolean called 'heat differs' is heat is not limit.
a boolean called 'limit differs' is limit is not heat.
Print "is not: {heat differs} {limit differs}".

a boolean called 'heat higher' is heat is greater than limit.
a boolean called 'limit higher' is limit is greater than heat.
Print "is greater than: {heat higher} {limit higher}".

a boolean called 'heat lower' is heat is less than or equal to limit.
a boolean called 'limit lower' is limit is less than or equal to heat.
Print "is less than or equal to: {heat lower} {limit lower}".

a boolean called 'both positive' is heat is positive and limit is greater than 5.
a boolean called 'both small' is limit is less than 5 and heat is positive.
Print "and: {both positive} {both small}".

a boolean called 'either six' is heat is 6 or limit is 6.
a boolean called 'neither six' is limit is 4 or heat is 6.
Print "or: {either six} {neither six}".

a boolean called 'heat unmatched' is not heat is limit.
a boolean called 'only one' is not heat is 4 and limit is 6.
Print "not: {heat unmatched} {only one}".

Set 'heat matches' to limit is limit.
Set 'limit matches' to heat is not heat.
Print "Set is: {heat matches} {limit matches}".

Set 'heat higher' to limit is greater than heat.
Set 'limit higher' to heat is greater than limit.
Print "Set is greater than: {heat higher} {limit higher}".

Set 'both positive' to limit is 6 and heat is 4.
Set 'either six' to heat is 5 or limit is 5.
Print "Set and, or: {both positive} {either six}".

Set 'only one' to not limit is 6.
Print "Set not: {only one}".
